 with that imp of a Jack being away ! They do be grown up after awhile an ' I s'pose you could n't have men if there were no boy babies", "context_len": 39}}}, "marshmallows": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Borden bought her a box of marshmallows and he had some illustrated papers", "context_len": 13}}}, "weaned": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "`` I 'm glad you did n't get weaned away , Marilla", "context_len": 12}}}, "bee": {"freq": 6, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "Shagbark had kept to a bee line from the last starting point to the emigrant camp", "context_len": 16}, "NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 4, "context": "He 's the king bee ! Only , just this , Harrington , you take care of me or I 'll blow the whole business", "context_len": 25}}}, "mollified": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 11, "context": "`` Oh , that was right Marilla , '' in a mollified tone", "context_len": 13}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 5, "context": "Cook , however , was mollified by Rosamund 's sweet face , and an excellent supper was packed in a hamper", "context_len": 21}}}, "spoons": {"freq": 10, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 10, "word_index": 47, "context": "The genie carried him into a treasury full of all manner of gold and silver and precious jewels past count or reckoning , price or estimation ; then he brought him into another place , where he saw all the requisites of the table , platters and spoons and ewers and basins and cups , of gold and silver , and thence to the kitchen , where he found cooks , [ 476 ] with their cooking-gear and utensils , all on like wise of gold and silver", "context_len": 88}}}, "crumbed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 15, "context": "Then she gave the babies a crust of bread to stop their clamoring while she crumbed up some in the saucepan and kept stirring it so that it should n't scorch , 