: "Rows of cottages and gardens , great corn and hayfields , stubble where cattle were browsing , enclosures of fattening pigs whose squealing had a mirthful sound", "context_len": 27}}}, "stubble": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 18, "context": "One Saturday afternoon Peggy had had a long scramble through copse and bracken , over fences and along stubble fields , and had filled her big basket almost full , somewhat to the detriment of her costume and fingers , and she was now working her way home along the edge of the pasture , picking as she went", "context_len": 59}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 23, "context": "He was a rather stout , low-browed man , with a very red nose and a shaven face , upon which a rough stubble of beard had begun to grow", "context_len": 30}}}, "thriftless": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "`` A bit of Europe on one of our islands and really a lesson to our own thriftless poor", "context_len": 19}}}, "horsey": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 18, "context": "But Pansy woke when her father stood her down , and said , rather drowsily -- '' Nice horsey ; '' and sat squarely down in the path", "context_len": 28}}}, "droop": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "The ladies came back and Violet began to nod and let her eyes droop", "context_len": 14}, "VERB": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 44, "context": "Hafed would have taken up every flower from his own garden and transplanted it to those of his `` Missy 's , '' if the other boys had not made him understand that this would be useless , and most of them would only droop and die", "context_len": 47}}}, "dit": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "`` Ont to dit down", "context_len": 5}}}, "gesticulated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "But Pansy made a great fuss and gesticulated furiously with her little fists", "context_len": 13}}}, "tantrum": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 21, "context": "`` Oh , my ! '' was the girl 's response ; `` wo n't you find Miss Irene in a tantrum this afternoon ! Do you mean to say you are going there ? And on Sunday , too ! ''", "context_len": 42}}}, "jolliness": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 14, "context": "There were bits of fun and queer sayings interspersed that made a sort of jolliness in her face", "context_len": 18}}}, "ovens": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 20, "context": "There was a great sand heap where the smaller children went to play and tumble about and build forts and ovens and sometimes sand each other", "context_len": 26}}}, "caboose": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "`` Get away from here with this big caboose of yourn ! '' said a rough voice , `` you take up too much room , '' and he wheeled the carriage around so suddenly the babies almost toppled over", "context_len": 40}}}, "greensward": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "When the throng moved about a little she could see the white fairy figures floating over the greensward , and hear the music that set one 's nerves a-tingle", "context_len": 29}}}, "unsubstantial": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 7, "context": "That was why the glories were so unsubstantial , and why the dream must end at midnight", "context_len": 17}}}, "seasides": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 33, "context": "Bridget had scoured and scrubbed and polished windows largely to pass away time , for the people next door had been away as well and the maids on a vacation earning money at seasides", "context_len": 34}}}, "cackle": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 42, "context": "It 's nice to be in your own place , though the folks where I staid were very good and pleasant , I s'pose they thought I might remember them in my will , '' and she gave a shrill sort of cackle", "context_len": 43}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Hush ! do n't cackle nor cluck", "context_len": 7}}}, "drowsing": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "It 's just a kind of drowsing life away", "context_len": 9}}}, "flummery": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Now tell me what you did ! My , but this toast tastes good ! Better than all their flummery", "context_len": 20}}}, "leavings": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 38, "context": "When the young animal drew back at last with a satisfied air , some hens who had been waiting politely came forward , and leaning far over dipped their beaks in the pan to drink up Lammie-noo 's leavings", "context_len": 39}}}, "shoveled": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 61, "context": "`` Oh , Bridget , such a kitchen and such a table , and no white cloth on it ! They , the servants did n't seem to care , and they were nice and clean at the Home , and you 're -- well , you have things as nice as in the dining room , and to have things shoveled out of the kettle on your plate or cold on a dish ! Sometimes puddings were good , and the creams and frozen things were clean and nice", "context_len": 90}}}, "tasty": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 23, "context": "Since we \u2019 re so near to land we can afford to use some of our still \u2019 s fuel to broil a tasty fish dinner", "context_len": 26}}}, "huff": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 25, "context": "And you know , Helen , if you ask me , I think it is all your fault that Hal went off in such a huff", "context_len": 26}}}, "burner": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 25, "context": "And no doubt I 'll fall asleep -- I always snore a little at first , and when you hear that you may light the burner in the other room and turn it very low and put the window down from the top and skip off to yourself", "context_len": 48}}}, "brant": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Brant a few times at Bayside", "context_len": 6}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Brant appears to be a nice , brisk fellow and it is lucky for Davis as well", "context_len": 17}}}, "wheeler": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Wheeler", "context_len": 1}}}, "scratchy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "`` And I do n't want this scratchy flannel on ! I like the other better ; ca n't I pull it off ? ''", "context_len": 25}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Whew ! is n't the grass scratchy on your legs ! '", "context_len": 12}}}, "eruption": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 15, "context": "The water was impregnated with sulphur and salt , and though there was not an eruption when the writer was present , there were marks on surrounding trees showing where mud had been hurled to a height of thirty or forty feet", "context_len": 42}}}, "thitherward": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "Which way should she go ? Her heart cried softly for Loraine place and almost unconsciously her feet turned thitherward", "context_len": 20}}}, "faucet": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 17, "context": "I did n't like the house so well and there was no bath only a cold water faucet and a gas stove , and I missed Bridget so much", "context_len": 29}}}, "fumigate": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Then the men came to fumigate the house and they all went to a friend 's and took lunch", "context_len": 19}}}, "hoods": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 24, "context": "Now she lifted them in the carriage , tucked them in with the pretty robe and they did look picturesque in their fluffy white hoods and fur cloaks", "context_len": 28}}}, "disturbs": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "Remember the noise disturbs Aunt Hetty", "context_len": 6}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "I 'll see that nobody disturbs you", "context_len": 7}}}, "possum": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "`` I fixed you that time ! Come , you ca n't play possum over me , get up ! ''", "context_len": 21}}}, "bridget": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Bridget walked up stairs very deliberately , `` Oh , Holy Mother of God ! Get up , children", "context_len": 19}}}, "seymour": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Seymour to talk through that funnel , and then Miss Armitage and the doctor , '' went on Bridget", "context_len": 19}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 0, "context": "Seymour", "context_len": 1}}}, "restoratives": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 5, "context": "Seymour had been trying various restoratives", "context_len": 6}}}, "rale": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 2, "context": "She 's rale poorly , now I tell you , an ' this child 's been looking after her as well as the babies", "context_len": 24}}}, "ungentle": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 41, "context": "Peggy was so amazed by the suddenness of the attack that for the moment she offered no resistance ; but , finding a storm of blows descending on her head like hail , she managed to squirm out of Betsy 's ungentle grasp , and fled after Bobby down the lane , followed by a shower of epithets from the gate , where the old woman stood shaking her fist until long after the children were out of sight", "context_len": 79}}}, "foghorn": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 22, "context": "They were received with a burst of cheers , led by Bean Perkins , whose voice was more than ever like a foghorn", "context_len": 23}, "UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 26, "context": "`` Right down the line , now ! '' called Phil , and , as if the cheering contingent understood , Bean Perkins , with his foghorn voice , started the song : `` Take it to the Goal Posts , Boys ! ''", "context_len": 44}}}, "peppermints": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "See here , babies , '' and he disgorged a paper of peppermints that at once soothed broken hearts", "context_len": 19}}}, "gorging": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 2, "context": "Biddy was gorging herself behind a tree trunk , the juncos and thrushes were eating seeds and cake crumbs scattered over the lawn , while the rabbit with a bland air surveyed the pleasant scenery and regaled himself on juicy lettuce leaves", "context_len": 42}}}, "ethical": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 6, "context": "To improve themselves , to cultivate ethical virtues , to lend a hand to their neighbors all were included in the Junto \u2019 s lofty aims", "context_len": 26}}}, "sidelong": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 34, "context": "'Well , ' said Emily , twisting her slim hands nervously , 'if I must tell , I went back to the schoolroom before dinner for my pencil-box , and , ' with a sidelong look at Peggy , ' I noticed Margaret Vaughan putting a book inside Mary Hill 's desk", "context_len": 52}}}, "scabby": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 19, "context": "`` He may strap me if he likes , but I ai n't going to be called a snotnosed scabby sneak of a devil -- ''", "context_len": 26}}}, "shins": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 14, "context": "`` -- And he slapped me in the face , and I kicked his shins good , and then we fit and I give him a punch in the belly and a good bunk in the eye -- ''", "context_len": 39}}}, "peppermint": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "The peppermint must have been a sedative to nerves and stomach for the twins looked up with an angelic smile and went on house building", "context_len": 25}}}, "sedative": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "The peppermint must have been a sedative to nerves and stomach for the twins looked up with an angelic smile and went on house building", "context_len": 25}}}, "proffering": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresC": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Seymour went home after proffering her services if she should be needed through the night", "context_len": 15}}}, "bum": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 8, "context": "`` Why , that Patsy 's a reg'lar bum ! He 's called me names -- he plays hookey too , and he tried to trip me up and I give him a left-hander , and he called me a stinking pup and ever so many nasty names and then we went at it", "context_len": 54}, "VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "Or did you just want to be chummy ? If you came to bum gas , you \u2019 re out of luck , Blake", "context_len": 24}}}, "bleed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "He made my nose bleed , and I guess I gave him a black eye ; and I kicked his shins -- he 's got fat legs", "context_len": 27}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "`` My country 's wounds , inflicted by this man , yet bleed", "context_len": 13}}}, "organic": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 2, "context": "Perhaps no organic disease at present , and if she gets through the next two or three years safely all may go well with her", "context_len": 25}}}, "rut": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 25, "context": "Archie brings a breath of the new world with him , and outside interests which I hope may prevent me from falling into the narrow rut that is so often the fate of elderly spinsters in retired villages", "context_len": 38}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "As a wheel landed in a rut full of thick mud , their pace was momentarily retarded", "context_len": 17}}}, "foreclose": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "So when I had to foreclose here I made you this offer", "context_len": 12}}}, "executor": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "I 'm going to make you executor , so get some one else to write out the will", "context_len": 18}}}, "whims": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 6, "context": "There 'll be no time for whims and fancies , or even for lessons ; for there is to be an enormous tea-fight , as I call it , for the young folk of the parish in the schoolhouse this afternoon , and games afterwards , and recitations ; and if you , Rosamund , can recite as well as Lucy has described , why , you will be invaluable", "context_len": 70}, "VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "It would be interesting could we know what whims passed through the brain of the animal which was one of the most intelligent of his species", "context_len": 26}}}, "stringy": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "If Marilla only could make their hair curl ! It 's so stringy , and we have n't worried at Aunt Hetty for what she did or what she did n't do , and were n't snappy when she found fault", "context_len": 41}, "NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 12, "context": "`` I used to be quite handy at it ; not the stringy kind , either", "context_len": 16}}}, "seamstress": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 15, "context": "`` So , thinkin ' , I s'pose , 't was n't for a poor seamstress like me to be so extravagant , she says , 'Eggs are high this season , -- eight cents apiece", "context_len": 36}}}, "numbness": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 3, "context": "There was a numbness in it that gave place to pain as the blood began to pulse strongly through it , but Bomba knew that in a short time it would be as well as ever", "context_len": 36}, "UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "By degrees a numbness crept along Matt \u2019 s limbs , and a drowsiness enwrapped his brain", "context_len": 17}}}, "qualms": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 28, "context": "He began to feel ill long before he had half finished his first cigarette , and by the time he was half-way through the second the most painful qualms seized him , and forgetting the fort and the fight and everything else in his extreme misery he rolled over on the grass , and spent a most unhappy morning", "context_len": 59}}}, "carnations": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 44, "context": "This was a form of amusement which appealed far more to Miss Forster 's mind , for her flowers suffered much from drought in summer time , and she was a keen competitor at the local horticultural shows , exhibiting some of the largest carnations and the roundest dahlias in the neighbourhood", "context_len": 52}}}, "motherhood": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 36, "context": "During the remainder of the night they slept in each other 's arms , and much of the hardness and the wildness of Irene 's nature melted away during that sleep , and some of that motherhood which is the most blessed gift God can give to a girl visited her", "context_len": 51}}}, "slaps": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Violet is developing quite a temper and slaps her little nurse", "context_len": 11}, "NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 18, "context": "Why , everybody knew , Mamie , because your mamma made such an awful fuss about those little slaps", "context_len": 19}}}, "coquettish": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 10, "context": "The gestures , the roll of the eyes , the coquettish turn of the head was the daintiest thing you ever saw", "context_len": 22}}}, "pertly": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 66, "context": "Then she repeated -- 'Where are you going , my pretty maid ? ' and she had a little milk pail on her arm , and she managed to keep the two parts wonderfully distinct -- it was remarkable in a child not three years old , and when she said -- 'Then I wo n't marry you , my pretty maid ' and answered so pertly -- 'Nobody asked you , sir , she said , ' it would have done credit to an exhibition", "context_len": 86}}}, "bewails": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_PresT": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 1, "context": "Borden bewails it for the childrens ' sake", "context_len": 8}}}, "ensconced": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 5, "context": "Three minutes later they were ensconced in the old summer-house , where they sat very close to each other , Irene not talking much , and Rosamund wondering what was to become of her", "context_len": 34}}}, "bloated": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 8, "context": "`` Remembering old times when we were both bloated aristocrats , favorites with the gods", "context_len": 15}}}, "aristocrats": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 9, "context": "`` Remembering old times when we were both bloated aristocrats , favorites with the gods", "context_len": 15}}}, "thirties": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 16, "context": "There were three persons at the table , an elderly couple and a woman in the thirties", "context_len": 17}}}, "penurious": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 61, "context": "He was the black sheep of an otherwise respectable family , went off and spent his portion in riotous living , afterward bought a tract of ground above Harlem , turned hermit , raised geese and ducks and pigs , married and had three daughters and they in turn married , glad , I suppose , to get away from the penurious living", "context_len": 63}}}, "shanty": {"freq": 15, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 15, "word_index": 32, "context": "He made it a point to pass by the ruins of the old express shed , and he found there what he expected to find -- the missing flag from the switch shanty ; only the rod was bare , the little piece of red bunting having been burned away", "context_len": 50}}}, "syndicate": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 4, "context": "The meeting of the syndicate is called for to-night , at the office of Random & Griggs , said McGlory , and I don \u2019 t want those two bars until the last thing before the bank closes at three o \u2019 clock", "context_len": 43}}}, "eluded": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 21, "context": "But at length some of the deadly missiles fell where they could not be immediately reached , and one of these eluded the observation of the besieged until they saw a sheet of flame curl over the eaves beneath the roof , and play upon the surface of the huge beams above , until they suddenly started into flame", "context_len": 59}}}, "moneyed": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "Richards cared nothing at all for the moneyed end of life", "context_len": 11}, "VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "You 'd better go to some moneyed man -- like Major Sturgis , for instance", "context_len": 15}}}, "suburbs": {"freq": 5, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 5, "word_index": 74, "context": "Her three cousins -- Gwendolyn , Russell , and Belle -- had greeted her cordially as soon as the train drew up in a station which , for size and grandeur , surpassed her wildest dreams , and then escorted her between a bewildering panorama of flashing lights , brilliant shop windows , swiftly moving cars , and people in an endless stream to another depot , for her Uncle Robert resided in the suburbs", "context_len": 75}}}, "endowment": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 14, "context": "It had been a gift from a benevolently disposed woman , with a small endowment that was occasionally added to", "context_len": 20}}}, "mistresses": {"freq": 7, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 7, "word_index": 46, "context": "First , the mischievous puppy started a little black and white rabbit , and sent it scampering away as fast as its feet could carry it , rushing after it among all the underbrush and briars , and never heeding the coaxing calls of his little mistresses or the louder and sterner voices of their brothers ; then coming back he rushed into a brook which ran by the way , and after rolling himself in it till the water was dripping from his silky coat , he shook himself and sent a shower of drops over the clean white dresses of the little girls ; and then finding the hole of a wood-chuck , he began scratching and burying himself in the earth in a frenzy to", "context_len": 128}}}, "loth": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"UNK": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "She seemed rather loth to produce them but she could find no excuse", "context_len": 13}, "NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 1, "context": "Nothing loth to have a share in the afternoon 's fun , the children dropped from the wall , and each accommodated with one of Archie 's arms , they went the round of the fair in true village fashion", "context_len": 40}}}, "attestation": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 21, "context": "Joseph at Glastonbury , and can produce , in the time requisite for a messenger to go and return , an attestation to that effect", "context_len": 25}}}, "corroboration": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 4, "context": "Everything was ready for corroboration", "context_len": 5}}}, "lorimer": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 0, "context": "Lorimer gathered up the important papers", "context_len": 6}}}, "gainer": {"freq": 2, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 2, "word_index": 5, "context": "Hayden was the principal ground gainer , and it was Stone who provided effective interference in assisting him to make his greatest distances", "context_len": 23}}}, "haired": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 7, "context": "He was a somewhat feeble , white haired old man but received them very graciously and was much interested in the story", "context_len": 22}}}, "affidavit": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 17, "context": "You can help the deal along by taking the bullion to these capitalists , along with my affidavit -- which is with the bars -- stating that the gold came out of a week \u2019 s run at the Pauper \u2019 s Dream \u2019 with our little ten-stamp mill", "context_len": 49}}}, "holmes": {"freq": 3, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 3, "word_index": 0, "context": "Holmes said she really smiled , and then a horrible thing happened , like a fit , and her mouth all curled up and her eyes rolled up to the whites and Marilla screamed and fainted and the old lady was dead in a minute , and then the child fainted several times and they put her in her own bed -- we 'd had her down stairs", "context_len": 68}}}, "undertaker": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 3, "context": "There 's the undertaker -- ''", "context_len": 6}}}, "pillowed": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB_Past": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "A very wan little girl was pillowed upon the lounge", "context_len": 10}}}, "economize": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"VERB": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 13, "context": "And now that the house is clear I feel that we need n't economize so closely", "context_len": 16}}}, "indentures": {"freq": 1, "POS": {"NOUN_P": {"freq": 1, "word_index": 6, "context": "Johnson received back Marilla Bond 's indentures with no remonstrance or objection", "context_len": 12}}}, "remonstrance": {"freq": 4, "POS": {"NOUN": {"freq": 4, "word_index": 16, "context": "There is no need to say anything , dearie , ' and she kissed away the remonstrance that was forming on Pauline 's lips", "context_len": 24}}}, "fervor": {"freq": 3, 